{"repositoryId":680982520,"availability":"available","full":"scottgriv/PWA-Demo-App","name":"PWA-Demo-App","description":"A Progressive Web App (PWA) demo that uses React, TypeScript, Node.js, Postgresql, and Scss/Sass/Less. Learn about PWAs and achieving a perfect Lighthouse score.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":7,"created":"2023-08-21T02:20:56Z","updated":"2026-09-02T00:20:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://scottgriv.github.io/PWA-Demo-App/","topics":["html","javascript","less","lighthouse","postgresql","postgresql-database","pwa","pwa-app","pwa-apps","pwa-boilerplate","pwa-example","react","sass","scss","sql","typescript"],"demo":"https://scottgriv.github.io/PWA-Demo-App/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:48.885Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:48.885Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:48.885Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:47:14.498Z","stars":6,"forks":7},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:47:48.885Z","stars":6,"forks":7}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PWA stands for Progressive Web App, which is a type of software application built using standard web technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript that functions like both a website and a mobile app.","This project showcases the cutting-edge capabilities of PWA web technology by utilizing a robust stack including React, TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL, and styling with Scss/Sass/Less. Designed as both an educational tool and a practical demonstration, it guides users through the intricacies of building a high-performance PWA capable of achieving a perfect Google Lighthouse score.","The project not only highlights best practices for web development and performance optimization but also offers insights into creating seamless, app-like experiences on the web, making it an invaluable resource for developers looking to enhance their skills in crafting modern, efficient web applications."],"